{"id":"chatcmpl-2d98fd88-9dbb-4d47-b6f0-bad660ab208d","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246230,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task required distinguishing between left vs. right thoracic scoliosis from a chest X-ray by determining the direction of spinal convexity. The successful strategy combined a specialized domain tool query with an explicit verification step against original image pixels before committing to an answer. The key insight is that directional/laterality findings must be confirmed using anatomical orientation cues (e.g., side markers) rather than trusting a single model's claim.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"For laterality or directional findings (left/right, medial/lateral), explicitly query the direction of the abnormality rather than just its presence.\",\n    \"When a specialized tool returns a claim, add a verification step against original image pixels before finalizing, especially for single-model outputs.\",\n    \"Use anatomical orientation markers (side markers, rib prominence, organ situs) to confirm which side is which before interpreting curvature or asymmetry.\",\n    \"Translate the diagnostic question into a mechanistic description request (e.g., 'which side is the convexity directed toward') to make the visual evidence directly answerable.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Convert left/right diagnostic questions into direction-of-deformity queries, then confirm laterality using orientation markers before answering.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted visual QA\": \"Treat single-tool outputs as hypotheses; add an explicit verification pass against raw pixels for spatially directional claims.\",\n    \"Ambiguous laterality tasks\": \"Anchor left/right judgments to independent orientation cues (markers, anatomical landmarks) rather than relying on model confidence alone.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm image orientation (side markers, anatomical landmarks) before assigning left vs. right.\",\n    \"Cross-check the directional finding against original pixels when only one model/tool supports it.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":485,"total_tokens":856,"completion_tokens":371,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":485},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":371}}}